# Line endings, decided here rather than by whoever cloned the repository.
#
# The external audit reported three extract parsers failing on CRLF input. The
# mechanism was real — a parser that splits on "\n" leaves a trailing "\r" on
# every line, so a heading match, a table cell or a keyword name silently
# carries an invisible character — but the scope was wider than the three files
# it named: nineteen scripts split on a bare newline.
#
# Two halves to the fix. This file stops CRLF entering the working tree in the
# first place; `scripts/lib/lines.mjs` makes the parsers survive it anyway, for
# input that does not come from git — a PDF extraction, a download, a file a
# contributor pastes in from Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never normalise these. Git's heuristic is good but not perfect, and a byte
# it "fixes" inside a PDF or a PNG corrupts the file.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip   binary
